                Some powders mention creatine in their marketing but list only a small amount, or fold it into a proprietary blend with no figure. The research supports 3 to 5 g of creatine monohydrate a day. Turn the tub around and look for a gram figure for creatine monohydrate in the Supplement Facts panel before you pay a premium for it.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Taking creatine only on training days</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Creatine works by keeping muscle stores full, which needs daily intake. If your blended shake is a training-day habit, your rest days get no creatine and your stores fill more slowly. Either drink the shake daily or keep a separate tub of creatine monohydrate for the days you skip protein.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Doubling up with two blended shakes</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
